<a href="mailto:aminns@uidaho.edu"><b>Dr. Tony Minns</b></a> is a UI visiting professor from the International Institute for Infrastructural, Hydraulic, and Environmental Engineering (IHE) in Delft, The Netherlands.  His expertise is in mathematical and environmental modeling with emphasis in river processes and water quality.  He will be living in Boise for one year and will be performing the hydrologic and geomorphic modeling for our project.
<p>
<b>Kim Sherwood</b> is the new hydrologist located at the Elk City Ranger District.  He takes Meg Foltz's place on our TAC and comes from western Washington where he worked as a hydrologic and forestry technician for the city of Seattle municipal watershed.

